# Notifications

Every toast and every delete confirmation goes through `useNotify()`
(`src/components/notifications/notificationContext.ts`). Only
`NotificationProvider.tsx` may use `ToastQueue` or `ToastContainer`. The rules
themselves live in code (`src/features/notifications/policy.ts`); this file
explains them.

## Which UI to use

| User action | UI | Call |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Edits a value (name, number, color, toggle) | None. The Changes badge counts it | plain setter, or `notify.edit(run)` to report failures |
| Adds an item (structure, component, scale, palette color, surface, mode set, formula, rule, interpolation, …) | Positive toast, no action | `notify.added(kind, run)` |
| Creates a registry term as a side effect | Folded into the add toast; on its own, "Term added to registry" | automatic |
| Adds or removes a small part (layer, element, property, binding, option, shadow layer, color stop) | None. Changes is the undo path | `notify.remove({ kind: <part kind>, … })` or plain setter |
| Deletes an item that removes no exported names | Neutral toast with Undo | `notify.remove({ kind, run, undo })` |
| Deletes anything that removes exported design-data names (token, alias, component, term in use, token-generating scale) | Destructive alert dialog, then neutral toast with Undo | `notify.remove(...)`. The dialog is chosen automatically |
| Something fails | Negative toast | `notify.error(failure)` |
| Copies to clipboard | Neutral "Copied to clipboard" | `notify.copied()` |
| Discards or resets many edits | Destructive alert dialog, no toast | wrap the action in `notify.quietly` |

`notify.remove` dry-runs the delete on a throwaway store and counts the exported
token names it would remove. Any removed name means the dialog. Kinds with tier
`api` always confirm. So `run` must take the store it is given:
`run: (store) => store.set(removeXAtom, id)`. Use `local: true` when the delete
only touches local editor state, and `confirmed: true` when the caller already
showed its own dialog.

## Wording

- Toasts: noun plus past-tense verb, sentence case, no period. "Color scale
  added", "Rule deleted", "Color scale added with one new registry term".
- Dialog title: "Delete [thing]", never a question.
- Dialog body: "Deleting this removes [count] tokens from the design data
  output." or the kind's `impact` text.
- Dialog buttons: the primary button repeats the verb ("Delete", "Discard",
  "Reset"), and the secondary is "Cancel".
- Spell out zero to nine. Use numerals for 10 and up.

## Colors

- Positive: adds.
- Neutral: deletes and copies.
- Info: neutral status messages.
- Negative: errors only. Never use red for a successful delete.

## One notification per action

`notify` merges every notice raised inside one user action and shows only the
highest-priority one (error, then delete, then add, then info). A repeated
identical message replaces the visible toast. Never call two `notify` methods
for one click, and never toast from inside a store atom.

## Adding a new kind

Add a row to `NOTIFICATION_KINDS` in `policy.ts` with a noun and a tier
(`part`, `item`, or `api`). Give `api` kinds an `impact` sentence. Then use the
kind at the callsite.

## Enforcement

- `pnpm test:notifications` runs `tests/notifications.ts` (rules) and
  `tests/notification-usage.ts`. The usage check fails on `ToastQueue` outside
  the provider and on question-mark alert dialog titles.
- ESLint `no-restricted-imports` blocks `ToastQueue` and `ToastContainer`
  imports.
